// Every building a region can have. `cost` is billions, `days` the build time at a
// construction pace of one, `capacity_gain` what one finished building adds to the country's
// construction capacity - the speed every one of its sites works at (ConstructionCost.Pace: a
// day of work a day at capacity one, faster above it with diminishing returns up to
// ConstructionPaceCeiling, slower below it) - and `jobs` the millions of workers one of them asks
// for, the labour MarketSystem staffs the country's plant from. There is no GDP number here: a
// building's GDP is the market value of what it makes and sells, every week it stands (the
// `gdp_gain` this file used to carry was a one-off step the market took back within two months,
// and is no longer read). What a building makes and burns is not here either: it is its place in
// common/production, and the build list reads it from there.
{
  "Agriculture": {
    "name": "Agricultural complex",
    "cost": 0.45,
    "days": 120,
    "capacity_gain": 0.05,
    "jobs": 0.42,
    "description": "Farms. Grow food and some fertiliser (and rubber where it grows) and employ country people. Without fertiliser part of the harvest is lost."
  },
